# ---- 2.9.1: mpr_intersect, the OTHER cheap overlap entry point. It had no
# benchmark at all, which is exactly why 2.9.0 could repair gjk_intersect_3d's
# tangency handling and leave this one running the pre-2.9.0 body without any
# gate noticing -- neither a test nor a number covered it. The 2.9.1 repair
# routes its no-portal path through gjk_intersect_3d, which costs one extra
# support evaluation on a separated pair: measured same-binary against the old
# body, median of min over 5 runs, box miss 1.452 -> 1.698 us (+17%), sphere miss
# 1.975 -> 2.360 (+19%), and the hit/tangency paths unchanged. The MISS row is
# the one to watch, for the same reason as its gjk sibling above.
# [measured: CHANGELOG.md 2.9.1 Performance, the same-binary A/B of the old and new mpr_intersect bodies]
#
